Subject: [PATCH] [upstream] avif: Add test image with an ICC profile that
 strict parsers reject
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Merge to release branch 7922 for M151.

Adds red-icc-version-zero.avif, a 3x3 AVIF whose 'colr' prof box
contains a 564-byte "sRGB IEC61966-2-1 black scaled" ICC profile whose
header declares an invalid version of 0.0, as emitted by Dropbox image
export pipelines and common in the wild. The Rust ICC parser (moxcms)
rejects this profile, while skcms accepts it. Since M150
(crrev.com/c/7755142) the Rust parser is the default, so AVIF decode
currently fails for such images (see bug).

Also adds a disabled unit test asserting that this image decodes with a
fallback to the CICP color description. The test is added disabled so
that the fix CLs can share the image and test; it will be enabled when
AVIF decode of this image is fixed, via the ICC parser accepting such
profiles (crrev.com/c/8138946) and/or an AVIFImageDecoder fallback to
the CICP color description (crrev.com/c/8127810).

Also adds Pierce Fortin to AUTHORS (first contribution).

R=wtc@google.com

    --gtest_also_run_disabled_tests reproduces the current decode
    failure.

